;==============================================================================
; Listing of src/MAC-14.BIN (HD6303X), base $C000. Comments: docs/asm/en/MAC-14.notes
;==============================================================================
; LEGEND MAC-14 (J88, Audi 100/200 typ 44, engine MC2)
; CPU HD63B03XP, ROM Fujitsu MBM27128 (16 KB, $C000-$FFFF), RAM $8000-$8290.
; External chip at address $0100/$0101 (register number / data): ADC, tooth counting,
; ignition, digital inputs. Its type has not been identified.
; Tick ≈ 10 ms [assumed, derived from the 5-baud receive code; tester tolerance ±10 %].
; Engine speed: 1 unit of $8018 ≈ 22…24 rpm [assumed], exact scale not confirmed.
; Port 2: P2DDR bit 1 = 1 makes all of P21-P27 outputs at once (HD6303X datasheet),
; so PORT2.5 (J17) and PORT2.6 (N75) work as outputs.
; Register $14 is RP5CR (RAM and port 5): bit 6 enables internal RAM $40-$FF,
; bit 7 is the RAM power-retention flag, bits 0/1 enable IRQ1/IRQ2. Tasks: 0 every tick,
; 1 every 2 ticks, 2 every 4, 3 every 10 (table D1E1).
;
; Code         What it is                           Pin    Where in the program
; F            brake light switch                   32     chip, reg. $19 bit 3 [assumed]
; F60          idle switch                          20     chip, reg. $19 bit 5 [assumed]
; F76          coolant thermo switch > 119 °C       14     PORT5.7 [assumed]
; F81          full load switch                     26     chip, reg. $19 bit 4 [assumed]
; G4           TDC sender (flywheel pin)            13/12  chip, IRQ1 events [assumed]
; G28          engine speed (ring gear teeth)       11/29  chip, reg. $0C/$0D -> $8018
; G39          oxygen sensor                        30     ADC ch. 3 (10 bit) -> $801C
; G40          Hall sender in distributor           27/25  PORT6.1 (input)
; G42          intake air temperature               24     ADC ch. 7 -> $8020 [assumed]
; G61, G66     knock sensors                        15,2/16 ADC ch. 6 via amplifier [assumed]
; G62          coolant temperature                  10     ADC ch. 2 -> $801B [assumed]
; G71          manifold pressure (inside the unit)  —      ADC ch. 0 -> $8019 [assumed]
; J17          fuel pump relay                      21     PORT6.6, 1 = on [assumed]: off without sync,
;                                                          on in test 4433 (F930), off by protections (EF60)
; J128         boost gauge in the instrument cluster 17    not found [?]
; J142         idle control unit (signal input)     4      ADC ch. 5 -> $801E (N65) [assumed]
; K66 / L      VEZ lamp, blink code output          31     PORT6.4
; N7           mixture frequency valve              8      timer output OC1, 71.8 Hz; test 4441 = 50 %
; N17          cold start valve                     1      PORT6.5, 0 = open; test 4443
; N65          fuel cut-off (via J142)              4      see J142
; N70          ignition power stage                 22     chip $0100 [assumed]
; N75          boost control valve                  19     PORT2.6, PWM in the CMI interrupt; test 4442
; N80          carbon canister purge valve          3      chip, reg. $0B: 00/FF slow PWM; test 4343
; N115         tank shut-off valve                  23     chip, reg. $19 bit 2; test 4331
; —            L line (diagnostic request input)    5      PORT5.6
; —            K line (KW1281)                      28     SCI (P23 receive / P24 transmit)
; —            coding (connector T6m)               6, 34  PORT6.2 and PORT5.4, which goes where is [?]
; —            supply voltage                       35     ADC ch. 1 -> $801A [assumed]
; —            "program running" signal (watchdog) —     PORT6.7, toggled every tick; if it stops, an external circuit restarts the CPU [assumed]
; —            tachometer, J142                     7      PORT6.3 [assumed]
; —            unknown output                       ?      PORT2.5: 1 at engine speed ≥ 20 units after sync, 1 after reset [?]
;
; Blink codes ($C928), two fault memory bits per code:
; 1111 ECU   2111 G28   2112 G4   2113 G40   2121 F60   2123 F81
; 2141/2143 knock retard limit   2142 G61   2144 G66
; 2214 overspeed   2221/2222 G71   2224 overboost
; 2312 G62   2322 G42   2342 lambda control   4444 no faults
; (code meanings are taken from an older analysis and will be rechecked against the code)
; Actuator tests ($C958): 4433 J17, 4441 N7, 4442 N75, 4443 N17, 4343 N80, 4331 N115.
; Test step order: the bit in $80AF shifts right: $80 J17, $40 N7, $20 N75,
; $10 N17, $08 N80, $04 N115 (verified for N7, N75, N17, N80, N115).
;------------------------------------------------------------------------------

